However, note that I made a slight adjustment to make it more idiomatic C#. 

Here's an improved and more exception-safe version:

```csharp
public void Save() 
{
    byte[] outBytes;
    string text = ToText();
    if (utf8Bom) 
    {
        var bom = new byte[] { 0xEF, 0xBB, 0xBF };
        outBytes = bom.Concat(Encoding.UTF8.GetBytes(text)).ToArray();
    } 
    else 
    {
        outBytes = Constants.Encode(text);
    }

    using var lf = new LockFile(GetFile());
    if (!lf.Lock()) 
        throw new LockFailedException(GetFile());

    try 
    {
        lf.SetNeedSnapshot(true);
        lf.Write(outBytes);
        if (!lf.Commit()) 
            throw new IOException(string.Format(JGitText.CannotCommitWriteTo, GetFile()));
    } 
    finally 
    {
        lf.Unlock();
    }

    snapshot = lf.GetCommitSnapshot();
    hash = Hash(outBytes);
    FireConfigChangedEvent();
}
```
The improved version disposes of `MemoryStream` as it's redundant, and utilizes C#'s `using` declaration for `LockFile`. Also utilizes `Concat` for concatenation of byte arrays.

